 "answer": {
  "text": "✓ Answered20.0s · 2 tool calls · 21 sources cited from 1 layer\n\nShow work ▾\n\nThe isolates are C236-11, 11-3677, 11-4404, 11-4522, 11-4623, 11-4632 C1, 11-4632 C2, 11-4632 C3, 11-4632 C4, 11-4632 C5, C227-11, Ec11-4988, Ec11-5603, Ec11-6006, 11-02030, 11-02033-1, 11-02092, 11-02093, 2011C-3493, and NA114.⁠1–20 I found 20 pathogen samples and 1 organism related to Escherichia coli.⁠1–20\n\nISOLATES AND THEIR AMR GENES\nC236-11⁠1\nSAMN00715300\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-3677⁠2\nSAMN00715303\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4404⁠3\nSAMN00715305\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4522⁠4\nSAMN00715306\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4623⁠5\nSAMN00715307\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4632 C1⁠6\nSAMN00715308\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4632 C2⁠7\nSAMN00715309\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4632 C3⁠8\nSAMN00715310\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4632 C4⁠9\nSAMN00715311\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\n11-4632 C5⁠10\nSAMN00715312\nacrF, aph(3'')-Ib, aph(6)-Id, blaCTX-M-15, blaEC, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, gyrA_S83A=POINT, mdtM, sul1, sul2, tet(A)\nNot recorded\nShowing 1–10 of 20\n‹ Previous\nPage 1 of 2\nNext ›\nWHERE THIS ANSWER COMES FROM\nEscherichia coli⁠21\nNOTES\nPathogen Detection lists 141,360 Escherichia coli isolates with these genes; the first 20 in the snapshot are shown.\nSearching Escherichia coli isolates in Pathogen Detection for AMR genotypes starting blaCTX-M; blaTEM and blaSHV alleles were not searched: most are not ESBLs and the name alone cannot tell an ESBL allele from a narrow-spectrum one, so listing them would show isolates that do not carry an ESBL.\n\nThis is a research summary, not medical advice.\n\n▶\nSOURCES\n21\nBased on 21 sources cited",
